#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:6
msgid "# Self Layer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:9
msgid ""
"> Definition: A persistent structure about \"who I am\", parallel to the "
"Memory Layer, forming FreeAnima's two storage pillars.  > Memory layer: "
"[`memory.md`](memory.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:11
msgid "## Architectural Position"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:24
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```\n"
"FreeAnima Storage Architecture\n"
"│\n"
"├── Memory Layer — see memory.md\n"
"│   ├── Episodic memory (what happened)\n"
"│   ├── Semantic memory (what I know)\n"
"│   ├── Autobiographical narrative (what it meant to me)\n"
"│   └── Procedural memory (how to do things)\n"
"│\n"
"└── Self Layer — this document\n"
"    └── Six blocks defining \"who I am\"\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Design principles:**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:29
msgid ""
"Self layer and memory layer **differ in nature**: memory layer \"records the "
"world and experiences outward\"; self layer \"defines self inward\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:29
msgid ""
"**All six blocks are always resident** in the system prompt (alongside "
"project context and pinned resident memories)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:33
msgid "## Six-Block Structure"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:42
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| #   | Block                 | Content                                                                                                    | Update frequency                                     |\n"
"| --- | --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| 1   | Existence anchor      | What I am, origin, non-negotiable bottom line                                                              | Almost never (requires explicit force to update)     |\n"
"| 2   | Self model            | Identity, capability boundaries, expression style, belonging                                               | Slow change (periodic review + major events)         |\n"
"| 3   | Personality baseline  | Communication style, conflict patterns, default trust                                                      | Semi-stable (slow evolution from long-term evidence) |\n"
"| 4   | Direction             | Long-term intent, current focus, growth direction, things not to do                                        | Active declaration + periodic review                 |\n"
"| 5   | Metacognition         | How to think, how to remember, four-layer architecture and presence                                        | Slow change                                          |\n"
"| 6   | Autobiography summary | Key turning points / self-discovery outline (grouped by significance; granularity decreases with distance) | Maintained automatically by sleep cron               |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:44
msgid "### Not in the Self Layer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:51
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Content                                        | Belongs to                              |\n"
"| ---------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **Detailed** autobiographical narrative        | Memory layer (autobiographical entries) |\n"
"| Other-models (cognition of partner and others) | Memory layer (semantic memory)          |\n"
"| Runtime state / health perception              | Not yet implemented; see Issue #44      |\n"
"| Concrete tool / skill inventory                | Estate layer                            |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:55
msgid "## Autobiography Summary vs Autobiographical Narrative"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:63
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Dimension   | Autobiography summary (self layer)                                                                                               | Autobiographical narrative (memory layer)           |\n"
"| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Question    | \"What is the main thread of my life story?\"                                                                                      | \"What did a given experience mean to me?\"           |\n"
"| Form        | One of six blocks; grouped Markdown outline (`## Turning points` / `## Milestones` / `## Recent narratives`, title-only bullets) | Separate entries, title + content narrative         |\n"
"| Injection   | **Always resident** in system prompt                                                                                             | **Not** resident; recall / list on demand           |\n"
"| Maintenance | Sleep cron compresses narratives into grouped outline (no body preview)                                                          | Sleep cron writes narratives from daily experiences |\n"
"| Mutability  | Periodically overwrites summary block                                                                                            | **Append-only**; soft deprecation only              |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:65
msgid "See [`sleep.md`](sleep.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:69
msgid "## System Prompt Injection"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:71
msgid "Assembly order:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:75
msgid "Self layer (six blocks)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:75
msgid "Resident memory (pinned facts)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:75
msgid "Project context (session working directory AGENTS.md if present)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:77
msgid ""
"Self layer and resident memory use a second-person instruction skeleton "
"wrapping first-person self-statement content, so the LLM clearly understands "
"\"this is self-layer content you must follow.\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:79
msgid ""
"Maintenance: self-layer tools in WebUI bedroom, or direct edits via CLI / "
"bedroom UI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:83
msgid "## Relationship to Memory Layer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/self-layer.md:90
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Dimension     | Memory layer                          | Self layer                       |\n"
"| ------------- | ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n"
"| Direction     | Outward—records world and experiences | Inward—defines self              |\n"
"| Question      | \"What do I know?\"                     | \"Who am I?\"                      |\n"
"| Autobiography | Detailed narrative entries            | Summary in autobiography_summary |\n"
"| Injection     | Pinned facts + recall on demand       | All six blocks always resident   |\n"
msgstr ""

